      "problem": "If $Y=\\{0\\}$, then $P(Y)=$",
      "worked_solution": "The power set of $Y,$ denoted $P(Y),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $Y,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list out the subsets of $Y:$\n\n- The subset with no elements is $∅.$\n\n- The subset with $1$ element is $Y$ itself: $\\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y)=\\{∅,\\{0\\}\\}.\n$$",
